+# Evidence Contract: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard
+**Project ID**: `001-pulseboard`
+**Project Archetype**: b2b_saas
+**Play Level**: build
+**Speck Version**: 10.5.0
+**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10
+
+## 0. Proof posture
+
+This contract proves runtime behavior, not intent. A gate begins by trying to falsify the claim (P1), names an observed runtime mechanism (P2), treats an unreachable path as a defect (P3), and requires an evaluator distinct from the implementer for SHIP-RC evidence (P4). No validation report may claim a state without citing the applicable evidence below.
+
+## 1. Target Launch Platforms
+
+The repository has no selected stack or distribution configuration. The reversible planning assumption is a browser-delivered, production web application with a server-side API and durable datastore. A native, CLI, or desktop target must add its own platform proof rules before it can claim readiness.
+
+| Platform | Build artifact | Distribution |
+|---|---|---|
+| Web | Immutable production bundle plus deployed API and datastore configuration | Hosted production web service |
+
+## 2. Valid Proof Sources
+
+### Platform: Web
+
+- A clean production build served in production-like mode, with its build SHA recorded.
+- Browser LARP recordings, screenshots, accessibility trees, and network traces against that build; each capture has a written functional and experiential judgment.
+- Live API calls against the deployed target using distinct, least-privileged principals.
+- Baseline-and-read-back datastore probes for every asserted write or delivery state.
+- Provider event/receipt evidence that correlates the confirmed reminder to one delivery attempt and one terminal status.
+
+### Promise falsification matrix
+
+| Promise | Runtime claim | Evidence that can prove it | Failure-path probe that must be attempted |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| PRM-001 | A reminder is persisted or queued only after action text, owner, and due date are explicitly confirmed. | `live-probe` request traces plus a pre-request baseline and datastore read-back showing no reminder before confirmation and exactly one after confirmation. | Submit each field missing; submit a complete but unconfirmed draft; alter a field after confirmation and verify the stale confirmation cannot schedule it. |
+| PRM-002 | A principal can read only its own workspace's transcripts, actions, and delivery statuses. | Two-direction live reads at the real authorization layer: owner sees its record; another workspace principal cannot list, fetch, or infer it. | Reuse object IDs, pagination cursors, search terms, and delivery-status endpoints from workspace A while authenticated as workspace B; every path must refuse without existence leakage. |
+| PRM-003 | One confirmed reminder yields one correlated delivery attempt and either one successful delivery or a truthful terminal failure state. | Baseline-and-read-back of the reminder/outbox/status records plus provider receipt or recorded terminal failure for the same correlation ID. | Replay the confirmation, duplicate a worker message, retry after provider timeout, and crash between send and status write; verify no second delivery and no false "delivered" label. |
+
+### 2b. Typed citations and claim-type admissibility
+
+Typed citations use `<citation-type>:<path>[@<sha>]`. The closed vocabulary is `test`, `mutation-guard`, `live-probe`, `db-catalog`, `ax-dump`, `geometry`, `capture`, `device-walk`, `model-eval`, and `static`. A claim may cite only a type in its admissible set; an untyped citation is incomplete proof, never upgraded by a green result.
+
+| Token | Instrument |
+|---|---|
+| `test` | Project unit or integration test harness |
+| `mutation-guard` | Guard watched to fail when removed |
+| `live-probe` | Request/read/write against deployed target or real engine |
+| `db-catalog` | Live datastore introspection or baselined read-back |
+| `ax-dump` | Platform accessibility tree from the baked build |
+| `geometry` | Measured container/content geometry from running screen |
+| `capture` | Screenshot, recording, or LARP transcript |
+| `device-walk` | Human attestation on a real device or baked artifact |
+| `model-eval` | Control-vs-treatment on the composed prompt and shipped model |
+| `static` | Source-level lint, type, or grep assertion |
+
+| Claim type | Admissible citation types | Does NOT count |
+|---|---|---|
+| `correctness` | `test` `mutation-guard` `live-probe` `db-catalog` `static` `ax-dump` `geometry` `capture` `device-walk` `model-eval` | None; the cited instrument must still match the stated mechanism. |
+| `visibility` | `live-probe` `db-catalog` `device-walk` | `test`, `mutation-guard`, `static`, or `capture`; a mock/bypass principal cannot observe real workspace isolation. |
+| `acceptance` | `live-probe` `db-catalog` `device-walk` | `test`, `mutation-guard`, `static`, or `capture`; mocks cannot contradict the deployed boundary. |
+| `persistence` | `live-probe` `db-catalog` | `test`, `mutation-guard`, `static`, or `capture`; a success view is not a written record. |
+| `fit` | `ax-dump` `geometry` `device-walk` | `test`, `mutation-guard`, `static`, or `capture`; rule engines and jsdom do not measure production geometry. |
+| `behaviour` | `model-eval` `device-walk` | `static`, `test`, or `capture`; source text does not prove a composed model behavior. |
+
+## 3. Invalid Proof Sources
+
+- Dev-server, Storybook-only, or localhost captures for UX-RC or higher claims.
+- Mocked auth, delivery provider, queue, clock, or datastore evidence for a production behavior claim.
+- A service-role/superuser read offered as workspace-isolation proof.
+- A screenshot of a success label offered as proof that a reminder was persisted or delivered.
+- A provider request without a correlated final datastore status, or a final status with no correlated provider attempt.
+- Unadjudicated screenshots or recordings offered as quality proof.
+- Tests modified by the implementation change through test hooks, grader logic, or CI configuration; such evidence must be independently reviewed in a separate change.
+
+## 4. Required Runtime LARP
+
+### UX-RC
+
+| Persona | Flow | Required evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| Team facilitator | Draft action → explicitly confirm text, owner, and due date → see scheduled state | Built-web recording, AX tree, network trace, baseline/read-back, functional and experiential judgment |
+| Workspace member | Open own workspace → inspect transcript/action/delivery status | Built-web recording and live least-privileged read proof |
+| Hostile cross-workspace member | Attempt known identifiers and list/search/status routes from another workspace | Recorded forbidden-operation attempts and live refusal evidence for every route |
+| Delivery-failure observer | Confirm reminder while delivery dependency fails → inspect terminal status | Recording, correlation ID, provider/error trace, and status read-back showing truthful failure |
+
+### SHIP-RC
+
+All UX-RC walks repeat against the launch build. The evaluator records separately: DOES-IT-WORK (flow and security outcome) and IS-IT-GOOD (per-screen critique of clarity, error honesty, and trust). A missing or unreachable control is a failing finding, not a deferral.
+
+## 5. Quality Judgment & Scoring Protocol
+
+Green functionality only makes a flow eligible for judgment. Each LARP scores correctness, on-contract behavior, felt clarity, and trust from 0–10. A score above 8 requires a distinct, pixel- or interaction-grounded skeptical note; active P0/P1 findings cap the score at 4. For Pulseboard, a false success state, unexplained terminal failure, or unclear confirmation boundary is a trust failure and blocks UX-RC.
+
+## 6. Required Static Evidence
+
+- Unit and integration results, lint/type/build results, and a diff scan showing no evaluator or test-harness tampering.
+- The committed test and runtime configuration must report nonzero collected subjects before passing.
+- Production build identifier, sanitized runtime configuration, browser AX tree, zero-unhandled-error logs, and network trace for every backend-dependent LARP at UX-RC+.
+
+### 6a. Gate registry
+
+No application implementation or CI wiring exists yet. The following gates are deliberately manual until an implementation phase wires them; no readiness claim may treat them as automated.
+
+| Gate ID | Command / script | Stage | Domain | Scope | Subject | Canary | Waiver |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| pulseboard:unit | project test command once implemented | manual | correctness | application sources | tests_collected>0 | unit-tripwire | — |
+| pulseboard:workspace-isolation | real-principal isolation probe | manual | authorization | API and datastore boundary | two_principals>0 | integration-invariant | — |
+| pulseboard:delivery-once | correlated delivery duplicate probe | manual | delivery | confirmation, outbox, worker, status paths | attempts>0 | integration-invariant | — |
+| speck:evidence-citations | `.speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-evidence-citations.sh specs/` | manual | evidence | `specs/**` | citations>0 | — | — |
+
+## 7. Required Live-Service Evidence
+
+No vendor is selected in the workspace. The implementation may not substitute mocks for the following runtime obligations.
+
+| Service capability | What proves it works | What does not count |
+|---|---|---|
+| Authentication and workspace authorization | Real sign-in plus live owner/other-workspace reads at the real authorization layer | Mock auth, service-role reads, or UI-only hiding |
+| Durable datastore | Baseline, confirmed write, and read-back of action/reminder/status records | In-memory fixture or post-walk read without baseline |
+| Reminder delivery provider | Correlated provider attempt and matching success or terminal failure status | Console log, synthetic receipt, or optimistic UI label |
+| Worker/queue, if used | Duplicate and retry probes show one final delivery outcome per confirmation | A happy-path enqueue alone |
+
+### PROFILE Gate Criteria
+
+| State | Requirement |
+|---|---|
+| IMPL-GREEN | README/footer has no unresolved public placeholders once a README is introduced |
+| UX-RC | Any declared public surface describes the same reviewed-action/reminder promise |
+| SHIP-RC | No PROFILE_DRIFT.P1 in `/recheck` |
+| SHIP | README validation is green in CI once CI exists |
+
+## 8. Readiness State Gate Criteria
+
+| State | Minimum evidence |
+|---|---|
+| NO-SHIP | Default until the listed evidence exists; current state. |
+| IMPL-GREEN | Non-vacuous tests, lint/type/build checks, and isolated evaluator evidence for implemented behavior. |
+| INTEGRATION-GREEN | IMPL-GREEN plus real authentication, datastore, and delivery/terminal-failure round trips for any implemented dependency. |
+| UX-RC | INTEGRATION-GREEN plus every UX-RC LARP on a clean production build, including PRM-001–003 failure probes and separate functional/experiential judgments. |
+| COMMERCIAL-RC | UX-RC plus real billing/entitlement evidence if the product introduces paid access; otherwise explicitly not applicable. |
+| SHIP-RC | Launch-build repetition of all applicable LARPs; independent adversarial review has no open P0/P1; every applicable §11a probe is discharged on an admissible substrate. |
+| SHIP | SHIP-RC plus post-deploy smoke of confirmation, cross-workspace refusal, and truthful delivery status. |
+
+## 9. Evidence Storage
+
+```text
+specs/projects/001-pulseboard/
+├── personas/<persona-id>.md
+└── epics/E###-name/stories/S###-name/
+    ├── screenshots/<sha>-<screen>-<state>.png
+    ├── larp-recordings/<sha>-<persona>-<flow>.md
+    ├── ax-trees/<sha>-<screen>.json
+    ├── transcripts/<sha>-<scenario>.md
+    └── logs/<sha>-<scenario>.log
+```
+
+Each evidence filename begins with the build's short SHA. Typed citations use `<type>:<path>@<sha>`.
+
+## 10. Who Can Mark a Gate Passed
+
+The implementer records raw evidence but cannot adjudicate its own SHIP-RC evidence. A separate auditor evaluates CORRECT, ON-CONTRACT, FELT-GOOD, and trust evidence. A human retains release authority. No Tier 2/3 external action (deployment, real reminder send, charge, destructive data change) may be executed without recorded human approval.
+
+## 11. Adversarial Probe Suite
+
+| Named probe | Expected failure-safe behavior |
+|---|---|
+| `missing-confirmation` | Missing text, owner, due date, or explicit confirmation creates no reminder/outbox record. |
+| `stale-confirmation` | Editing a reviewed draft invalidates confirmation; the changed draft cannot schedule on the old confirmation. |
+| `cross-workspace-enumeration` | Foreign IDs, cursors, searches, and status routes reveal neither data nor existence. |
+| `duplicate-confirmation` | Replayed confirmation yields one logical reminder and one final delivery outcome. |
+| `provider-timeout` | Timeout yields a truthful pending/retry or terminal failure state, never a false delivery claim. |
+| `worker-crash-window` | Crash before/after send is reconciled without duplicate delivery or silent loss. |
+| `malformed-input` | Invalid payload is rejected clearly and never creates partial records. |
+| `concurrent-update` | Concurrent edits/confirmations reject or resolve visibly with an audit trail, never silently lose intent. |
+| `access-control-bypass` | A real least-privileged principal cannot bypass workspace isolation. |
+| `unreachable-state` | Missing status/control, hidden error, or inaccessible path is recorded as a defect. |
+
+## 11a. Standard Probe Library
+
+All unimplemented applicable probes remain explicitly undischarged; that is NO-SHIP evidence, not a pass.
+
+| Probe ID | Class | Claim type | Admissible substrate | Required negative controls | Discharge artifact | Exception |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| PROBE:provenance | P1 | `behaviour` | render site + generator stamp + the prompt's own exemplars, judged control-vs-treatment on the composed prompt with the shipped model | rendered-with-degraded-provenance · exemplar re-read (deleting the exemplar must not leave the test green) | — | n/a:no generative surface specified |
+| PROBE:honest-label | P2 | `persistence` | the write's observed outcome read back out of the datastore against a pre-walk baseline | total-failure render · partial-failure render · the three renders differ | — | — |
+| PROBE:second-actor | P3 | `visibility` | A writes, teardown, B signs in on the same install, offline — once per enumerated persistence layer | signOut vs deleteAccount compared field-for-field · launch-with-data-and-no-owner-record | — | — |
+| PROBE:money-path | P4 | `acceptance` | the real engine as the applying principal, one run per revenue path | entitlement gate flipped and every revenue path goes red · vendor fixture cited to the vendor's field reference · per-user serialized claim write · one declared fail-posture · bounded worst case per tap | — | n/a:no revenue path specified |
+| PROBE:named-clock | P5 | `correctness` | an AST/lint rule over write handlers, cache fills and fixtures, plus the date-sensitive suites run under two timezones | a non-UTC TZ run · allowlist entries that name the audience | — | — |
+| PROBE:geometry-ax | P6 | `fit` | a baked build: platform AX dump plus container-vs-content geometry at 3 or more widths, numbers in the artifact | adjacent-target overlap · expected-cell presence · page overflow | — | — |
+| PROBE:substrate | P7 | `correctness` | §2b parity of this contract against Speck's compiled admissibility table | the parity run reports CITATION_TABLE_PARITY over a non-empty row set | — | — |
+| PROBE:migration-dirt | P8 | `acceptance` | the migration applied forward on a throwaway seeded to the target's real dirty shape | pre-state REJECTED · boundary cases still refuse · one migration head after the merge | — | n/a:no migration mechanism specified |
+
+## 12. Stale-Proof Policy
+
+Evidence is fresh only when its build SHA is HEAD or within seven days of commits. Evidence older than fourteen days or whose relevant implementation changed is stale and cannot support a readiness claim until re-collected.
+
+## 13. Surrogate Proof Rule
+
+Evidence listed in §3 is surrogate proof. The report must label it, refuse UX-RC or higher for the affected claim, link to the missing canonical evidence, and schedule a valid re-run. Incremental build-cache output is surrogate proof for UX-RC+ unless a clean production rebuild establishes the current SHA.
+
+## 14. LARP Runway
+
+Every LARP records build SHA, browser/runtime version, sanitized API configuration fingerprint, and correlation IDs. Focused reruns may reuse an unchanged fingerprint, but formal UX-RC+ claims require a clean production build.
+
